    "about.kicker": "About me",
    "about.title": "Amir, a web developer in Astana",
    "about.p1": "I build websites in Astana for small businesses across Kazakhstan: cafés, shops, salons and independent specialists. I help present your services clearly and make it easy to get in touch from a phone.",
    "about.p2": "I work on my own, without an agency or account managers: you deal with me directly, which makes things faster and cuts the markup. What matters to me is that the site doesn’t just look good but actually brings you enquiries — which is why I ask more about your customers than about button colours.",
    "about.chip1": "Astana, Kazakhstan",
    "about.chip2": "Working across Kazakhstan",
    "about.chip3": "I reply within an hour",
    "about.chip4": "I speak Russian and Kazakh",
    "faq.kicker": "Common questions",
    "faq.title": "Any questions?",
    "faq.q1": "I know nothing about websites. Is that a problem?",
    "faq.a1": "No — that’s true of almost everyone. Knowing about websites is my job. You describe your business in ordinary words, I ask clear questions and handle all the technical decisions myself.",
    "faq.q2": "How much does a site cost?",
    "faq.a2": "A simple site starts at 30,000 ₸, a business site at 60,000 ₸, and a larger project with a basket and payments at 100,000 ₸. I’ll give you an exact figure after a short conversation. The price is fixed before work starts and doesn’t go up afterwards.",
    "faq.q3": "How long does it take?",
    "faq.a3": "Usually 3–5 days for a simple site and 7–10 days for a business site. Larger projects are agreed separately. Most of the time goes into your photos and copy — if those are ready, it’s faster.",
    "faq.q4": "What if I don’t like the design?",
    "faq.a4": "I show you how the site will look first, and we revise that as many times as needed. I only start building once you’ve approved it — so you never pay for something you don’t like.",
    "faq.q5": "What are a domain and hosting? Do I have to buy them?",
    "faq.a5": "The domain is what customers type into their browser, something like your-cafe.kz. You also need somewhere for the site to live. That’s paid once a year, separately, and it isn’t expensive. I’ll advise what to choose and set it all up — the payment stays in your name so the site always belongs to you.",
    "faq.q6": "Will I be able to change prices, photos and text myself?",
    "faq.a6": "Yes. If you need to change things often — a menu or a product list, say — I’ll build a simple admin panel: open it on your phone and update a price or photo in a minute. If changes are rare, you can just message me.",
    "faq.q7": "How does payment work?",
    "faq.a7": "Half at the start, the rest once the site is finished and you’re happy with it. By bank transfer or Kaspi, whichever suits you. Everything we agree is put in writing so it’s clear on both sides.",
    "faq.q8": "Do you only work in Astana?",
    "faq.a8": "I live in Astana but work with clients across Kazakhstan. WhatsApp is usually easiest — meeting in person isn’t necessary. If you’re in Astana and would like to meet, that’s fine too.",
    "faq.q9": "What happens to the site after launch?",
    "faq.a9": "The site is entirely yours. The first month of changes is free. After that, message me whenever you need — small fixes are usually done the same day.",
